=== A6 LEG 1: fit-table.md VERBATIM ===
# T196 — Measured-fit leg (A6, guard-measured-fit) · attempt 1 · Cycle 035

Stage 360 px wide (16:9 → stage height 202.5 px). Stage box bound by amendment A10: `stageBox` 88% × 62% → box 316.8 × 125.55 px. Measurement model: per-glyph advance widths (Helvetica/Arial-class metrics, fractions of em) summed over each card's actual CONFIG words + the CSS word margin (0.18 em × 2 per word); greedy word wrap inside the box; the build's own `fitCard` shrink loop (maxSizePx 64 → minSizePx 20, step 2) applies the same contract in-browser — REFILED at the Cycle-035 completion cure (jev-prewave HOLD cure): fitCard now probes each card laid out (display:flex, visibility:hidden — never display:none), includes the 0.36 em per-word margins in each word's ink, and wraps greedily per word, exactly this table's contract. Ink height = cap-height-class ink ≈ 0.72 × font size. PIXEL-UNVERIFIED seat (no browser binary): geometry is measured from glyph metrics, not from a rendered frame — printed limitation, carried to scores.md.

| Element | Container | Fitted size | Measured ink (full line, unwrapped) | Lines after wrap | Ink height | Total height vs box 125.55 px | Margin (binding side) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Card c1 "This system brings in varying" (5 spans) | stage box 316.8 × 125.55 | 40 px | 543 px | 2 | 28.8 px | 100.0 px ≤ 125.55 ✓ | 25.55 px vertical |
| Card c2 "types sizes, weights and animation," (5 spans) | stage box 316.8 × 125.55 | 32 px | 525 px | 2 | 23.0 px | 80.0 px ≤ 125.55 ✓ | 45.55 px vertical |
| Card c3 "so you can feel when my voice gets louder or softer" (11 spans) | stage box 316.8 × 125.55 | 32 px | 767 px | 3 | 23.0 px | 120.0 px ≤ 125.55 ✓ | 5.55 px vertical |
| HUD readout (non-subject, chrome) | stage bottom-left | 12 px monospace | — | 1 | ~8.6 px | n/a | n/a (not subject text) |

Legibility floor (~11 px ink at 360 px stage): all subject rows 23.0–28.8 px — above floor ✓.
Hierarchy: no size hierarchy is claimed between subject elements (D5 holds size constant across states and cards fit independently); state separation is color-only by construction, so the hue-only-hierarchy HIT class does not apply — the separation is instead discharged by the computed contrast floor + ΔE pair check in build-record.md (19.26 / 16.57 vs bg; ΔE 90.5 ≥ 30).

