    28	- FED: build-record.md · the CONFIG block of recreation.html · the technique's packet section · guards.md command list (what own-checks should exist) · **the item's A6 leg outputs (fit-table.md + config-census.md) — added 2026-11-16, recreation Cycle 024 Condense, on the Wave-21 pattern: prewave firings for T151, T153 and T154 all HOLDed or re-fired on feed completeness (the A6 files and packet section existed complete in the artifact directory but were not in the payload), the lane's recurring ASSERTED-CHECKS false-positive class. A payload lacking any FED element is a feeder defect, printed as such in the build record; a HOLD whose only named cure is feeding an already-filed FED element is disposed as a feed-completeness miss, with the miss recorded.**
    29	- FED (added 2026-11-17, Cycle 026 Condense — the T167 miss): **the wave record's binding census-anchor mapping for the item + any Observe dispositions pricing source ambiguities** (the §1d-form: where a packet caption or digest line admits two readings, the wave record's priced reading governs). A HOLD founded on a source ambiguity the wave record has already priced is a feeder defect, disposed as such in the build record — the judge prices the build against the binding mapping, not against raw source prose. (Founding miss: Cycle 026 T167 — HOLD priced a packet caption's ambiguous reading against a build that followed the gate-approved mapping; the seat upheld the set-aside at §5.)
