   186	=== PACKET SECTION (digest.md, T07) ===
   187	### T07 — Pre-lighting: the whole line visible before it is spoken (38–67 s, the demonstration sections throughout)
   188	- **Mechanics (the trick):** caption lines in the demonstration sections are FULLY VISIBLE from the line's first frame — future words are already on screen in white (the unspoken state), and each word's spoken onset changes its state (color flip in T06; size/weight in T08). At 55 s the line "so you can feel when my voice gets louder or softer" stands complete on screen with its spoken prefix yellow and "louder or softer" still white, BEFORE the size states those words will take. Anticipation is therefore a visibility state, not a reveal: nothing appears at onset; something CHANGES at onset. (The queue's learn-reason described this as words "pre-light in white before turning the speaker's color" — the frames confirm the white pre-state; what turns at onset in the narration demos is the spoken-state yellow, and in scene demos the speaker's color, T09.)
   189	- **Why it works:** the reader can pre-read the whole line (no word ever ambushes), while the state change still marks the voice's position — anticipation and synchronization in one device.
   190	- **Evidence:** ev/t055-line-before-ramp.jpg (the complete line visible, spoken prefix yellow, unspoken remainder white, before the ramp states) · ev/t044-sync-highlight-mid.jpg (the same state in the sync demo). Clip: clips/040-sync-highlight-7s.mp4 (the state changes are the clip's content).
   191	
