   842	     1	# T196 — Plan Amendment · Cycle 035 Wave 32 (filed BEFORE any build script, per A9.2 + wave RUN §2b)
   843	     2	
   844	     3	Source: jev-plan-exit REVISE (T196) + jev-observe-exit charges, consumed in wave RUN §2b. This amendment amends the Cycle-034 item record's Plan; the build executes the Plan AS AMENDED. The Cycle-034 record is not retro-edited (A8).
   845	     4	
   846	     5	## A1 — CP3b source-fidelity result (separate from the schedule assertions)
   847	     6	CP3b is a SOURCE-FIDELITY checkpoint, reported separately from CP3a's schedule result:
   848	     7	- Census state at source 55.0 s (ev/t055): prefix through "gets" spoken; "louder or softer" WHITE + unscaled.
   849	     8	- Build state at the corresponding instant (build 7,240 ms = source 55.0): the ASR-anchored schedule has "louder" (onset 6,880 ms) ALREADY SPOKEN.
   850	     9	- **Expected departure (priced, D3):** SOURCE-FIDELITY at CP3b = DEPARTURE-EXPECTED. The build follows the ASR onset series (the only complete onset series); the source's visual flip for "louder" lags ASR by >360 ms. CP3b does NOT pass as fidelity and does NOT fail the schedule: it is recorded as a named, priced departure. No revised visual onset is adopted for "louder" alone, because a single-word visual onset without the full per-word visual series would invent precision the census does not carry (D3 stays an explicit ASR-based approximation until visual flip times are measured).
   851	    10	
   852	    11	## A2 — Flip checks evaluate at onset + ε
   853	    12	Every flip assertion evaluates at `onsetMs + ε`, ε = 1 ms (CONFIG-derived where the onset is CONFIG). CP5a's strict `spoken iff onset < t` at exactly t = 8,640 ms is untestable as filed (at t = onset the tie rule yields UNSPOKEN); CP5a therefore evaluates at 8,641 ms. The tie rule itself (`spoken iff onsetMs < t`) is unchanged and is asserted separately at the exact onset instant (state = unspoken).
   854	    13	
   855	    14	## A3 — End sample / terminal state
   856	    15	CP5b evaluates at `totalMs − ε` (10,559 ms), inside card 3's half-open interval. Explicit terminal state: for t ≥ totalMs the stage holds card 3 fully spoken (the phase machine clamps to the final state); this terminal state is specified here and implemented as clamp, not as an interval extension.
   857	    16	
   858	    17	## A4 — Comparison uses ONE clock
   859	    18	The comparison expression uses file-local `currentTime` only, with the head handle: **core build zero ≡ video 0.5 s**. The segment is cut with a 0.5 s head handle (source 47.26 s) and a 0.5 s tail handle (source 58.82 s), duration 11.56 s. Mapping: `buildMs = (video.currentTime − 0.5) × 1000` (at timingScale 1). The 47.76 s source timestamp never appears in the comparison's clock expression; it appears only in the label and in this record.
   860	    19	
   861	    20	## A5 — The 28 ms all-white interval: LOGIC vs PAINTED-FRAME outcomes kept separate
   862	    21	CP1 reports two outcomes: (a) LOGIC — the state function at t = 5,032 ms yields card 3 with 11/11 spans present + unspoken (asserted mechanically); (b) PAINTED-FRAME — whether a painted frame in [5,032, 5,060) actually displayed the all-white card during continuous playback. This seat has no browser binary (PIXEL-UNVERIFIED, T132 precedent): PAINTED-FRAME = NOT EXERCISABLE IN THIS SEAT, recorded as such, never merged into the LOGIC result.
   863	    22	
   864	    23	## A6 — D2 act (observe-exit charge)
   865	    24	Before card 2's visual anchor is frozen, a frame-measurement refresh is run inside the 49–50 s bracket (frames at 49.60 / 49.70 / 49.78 / 49.90 / 50.00 s extracted from source.mp4 and viewed). The measured result is recorded in build-record.md; the anchor is frozen only from that measurement (or the bracket is narrowed and the residual named).
   866	    25	
   867	    26	## A7 — D3 status
   868	    27	D3 stays an explicit ASR-based approximation until per-word visual flip times are measured. No visual onset is claimed for any individual word.
   869	    28	
