   961	study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-034-wave-31/item-T196-observe-plan.md:14:Sibling T195 (same packet, this same wave, no scores yet) is the sweep's **color-state flip**: its subject is the change itself — white→yellow per word at spoken onset, sweeping at letter scale. **T196 is the visibility contract**: its subject is what is true *before* any change — the whole line present from the start in its unspoken state; only state changes at onset. A build that renders words progressively but flips them on time could satisfy T195 and would FAIL T196. T196's scored invariant: word-node count, visibility, and geometry are constant across every onset; only state classes change. The recreation's assertion suite (A11 map below) tests presence, not flip color.
